{
  "title": "Traumatic Spondylolisthesis of Axis (Hangman's Fracture)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/spine/2017/traumatic-spondylolisthesis-of-axis-hangmans-fracture",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 9 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Traumatic spondylolisthesis of the axis, also known as a Hangman's fracture, is a traumatic fracture of the bilateral pars interarticularis of C2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with CT of the cervical spine",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment may be C-collar immobilization, halo immobilization, or surgical stabilization depending on displacement, angulation, and fracture stability",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**hyperextension**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to fracture of the pars",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**secondary flexion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tears PLL and disc, allowing subluxation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated injuries",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "30% have concomitant C-spine fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "neck pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "patients are usually neurologically intact",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "flexion and extension views show subluxation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2017/images/hangman_s_lateral_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2017/images/hangman_s_lateral___flexion_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "study of choice to delineate fracture pattern",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRA",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "consider if suspicious of a vascular injury to the vertebral artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
